<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Turkish War (1735–1739)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1735">1735</a>–<a href="/years/1739">1739</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Turkish War of 1735–1739 was fought by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, joined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> from 1737, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the Crimean Khanate. Russian armies under Münnich invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, burning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhchysarai">Bakhchysarai</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azov">Azov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ochakiv">Ochakov</a> and won at Stavuchany in 1739, but losses to disease were heavy. By the Treaty of Niš of 1739 Russia regained Azov, which had to remain unfortified.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1735-1739.jpg" alt="Russo-Turkish War (1735–1739)" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anik Benoit · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_Ochakov_(1737).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
